schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Funding Your Gatherings
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: framework
  summary: >-
    A four-tier framework for funding local-node gatherings, from zero-budget
    (shared meals, free venues, skill contributions) through low ($10-100:
    member contributions, passing the hat, monthly dues), medium ($100-500:
    local business sponsorship, small grants, web3-native funding via Gitcoin
    Grants/Giveth/Endaoment) to large ($500+: ticket sales, tiered sponsors,
    speaker budgets, ecosystem grants like the Ethereum Foundation ESP).
    Core argument: start with the cheapest thing that works, be transparent
    about money, and don't outspend your community's actual capacity.
  audience: local regen node organizers planning their first gatherings
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      Recommends collecting contributions on-chain (multisig, Juicebox) as
      "the easiest real introduction to wallets your members will ever get" —
      a genuine convenience argument that also nudges a low-stakes social
      event toward on-chain tooling before it's strictly needed.
  related_concepts:
    - quadratic-funding
  related_resources:
    - gitcoin-grants
    - giveth
    - endaoment
    - juicebox
    - ethereum-foundation-ecosystem-support-program
    - octant
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/funding-gatherings.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

# assessed-but-excluded (wo-fbc6bfc6b3e0, funding-gatherings.md):
# - "Try This" exercise prompts (answer three budget questions, set up a
#   multisig for one event, build a six-month funding ladder) — reader
#   action items, not extractable knowledge-graph content.
# - The itemized 50-person event budget table (venue/food/materials/speaker
#   honoraria/AV/contingency at Low/Medium/High) — folded into the
#   encyclopedia summary as illustrative detail rather than split into a
#   separate object; it is a worked example of the tiers, not a distinct
#   concept or resource.
